A1. This may be Greek to some of you. ~ ETA
A4. What a government guest is, when given leave of absence. ~ PAROLED
A10. Some girls pass in this. ~ MOB
A13. This fellow is always hanging around poles. ~ BYRD
A15. In winter this saves wear and tear on the sofa. ~ SEDAN
A16. Don't get stuck in this. ~ MIRE
A17. One kind of bologney! ~ BROAD
A19. This supports many a man. ~ BED
A20. This fellow is generally kept on the bench. ~ JUDGE
A21. This one is liable to take you for a ride. ~ OMNIBUS
A23. This is sometimes made on a naughty night club. ~ FORAY
A25. There's lots of these in New York. ~ ACRES
A26. These are nice about the house. ~ MAIDS
A28. A form of verb "to be" ~ AM
A30. To add to—increase. ~ EKE
A31. This oath is not taken on a bible. ~ CURSE
A32. Baby's cry for it. ~ MA
A33. What Paddock did to get ahead. ~ RAN
A35. The wrong way to "get rich quickly." ~ STEAL
A37. This is a give-away. ~ TREAT
A39. To encourage. ~ ABET
A41. A factory has this as well as a sultan. ~ SIREN
A43. A bum cook gets this. ~ SENT
A44. Cops and conferences do this to you. ~ DETER
A46. Most people have trouble getting these into their head. ~ DOSES
A48. You can do this in bed but not in court ~ LIE
A49. A very common article in Spain. ~ EL
A50. One who tries to lay the law down to those who uphold it. ~ REBEL
A52. You should do this to this word in no time. ~ SEE
A54. A Metric meaure of area. (Abbr.) ~ AR
A55. This is a lot of bull. ~ STEER
A56. This word applies to some jokes, as well as doughnuts. ~ STALE
A58. What some "hams" aren't and some hams are. ~ SWIFT
A59. One important point about a compass. ~ EASTERN
A61. One reason I'd hate to lead a dog's life. ~ FLEAS
A62. This is good to swat flies. ~ BAT
A63. This always has to go around in circles to get any place. ~ SCREW
A65. Some poor fellows get hit for this. ~ LOAN
A66. The first women's club, and it was endowed by a man! ~ HAREM
A68. Separated by violence. No, sonny, not divorced! ~ TORE
A69. Still. ~ YET
A70. Don't ever do this if wifie asks you to walk a straight line some night. ~ MEANDER
A71. Fish come from them and they come from fish. ~ ROE

D1. This can move the mighty ocean. ~ EBB
D2. A beginner, a novice. ~ TYRO
D3. One thing you don't mind getting in the nose. ~ AROMA
D5. Like. ~ AS
D6. A close relative of what you are now trying to do. ~ REBUS
D7. These have been written to a Grecian urn and a lot of women. ~ ODES
D8. Practically every great man was this at one time. ~ LAD
D9. A printer's measure. ~ EN
D10. The luckiest king in history. Everything he touched turned to gold. ~ MIDAS
D11. A hot party, thrown every year, by the Greek bacchanals. ~ ORGY
D12. You may get stung on this. ~ BEE
D14. This is done, in your own shoes, in some other person's shoes, and sometimes on some other person's shoes. ~ DANCE
D16. These are simply killing! ~ MURDERS
D18. These often make a stab at things. ~ DIRKS
D20. This keeps the roof over our head. ~ JOIST
D22. These will probably get cooked. ~ BEETS
D23. The right side of a horse, but the wrong side to mount on. ~ FAR
D24. Official hiking parties. ~ PARADES
D26. These carry a lot of weight. ~ MULES
D27. Rags. ~ TATTERS
D29. This should be the name of somebody's girl friend. ~ MABEL
D31. Heard beneath Spanish balconies. ~ CAROL
D32. A kind of madness. ~ MANIA
D34. Some poor fish'll get caught on this. ~ NET
D36. An over-grown duck. ~ EIDER
D38. This is a rather slippery proposition. ~ EEL
D40. A fever. ~ TERTIAN
D42. These are generally up a tree. ~ NESTS
D45. Sailors often get stuck on these. ~ REEFS
D47. What do playgoers demand most at theatrical performances. ~ SEATS
D51. One thing a hen never lays. ~ BET
D53. Voters do this to most big officials. ~ ELECT
D55. A poor fish can't do this. ~ SWEAT
D56. Fed up. ~ SATED
D57. This one's easy to make. ~ ERROR
D58. A bitter plum for anyone to swallow. ~ SLOE
D59. The opposite of horizontal 35. ~ EARN
D60. A Roman Emperor. ~ NERO
D61. "Birds do it, bees do it . . ." ~ FLY
D62. What do the sheep say, Junior? ~ BAA
D64. Not much to this one. ~ WEE
D66. The kind of man flappers sigh for. ~ HE
D67. Personal pronoun. ~ ME


